# L §6.1 What same does: "A thing's entries are such facts: an entry only one side states stands, and on a day on which
# the two sides' entries into one kind disagree, whatever depends on the thing being alive there is a HOLE-SAME hole
# (in a binding over that kind, an unknown member, §5.11)"; L §5.10 "a leg into or out of a thing outside its lifespan
# is refused (RUN-LIFESPAN)". a.konto lives from 2026-01-01, b.konto from 2026-03-01; the gift (one movement, same
# a.gift = b.gift_seen) lands on 2026-02-15, where ana's side books it and ben's refuses it: in the joint model the
# balance is a HOLE-SAME hole naming both lifespans (k), and a binding over accounts on a day they disagree has an
# unknown member (n_feb); on a day both sides hold it alive the place counts once (n_jun). Each member alone: ana
# 100.00 + 200.00 = 300.00 PLN (a.q); ben refuses its gift's leg (b.q). (Was REFCORE-NOT-YET: places stated same whose
# lifespans differ.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "aa505bbd10874d87c91f67dc9f21660373d7e31c463a18bd8f40be78555393d7"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "d5e54917a9117b52aa138246f6473084a0676e2515e02cb4a44693b52a921e53"
  same a.konto = b.konto
  same a.gift = b.gift_seen
  same a.pay = b.pay_seen

ask k: bal(a.konto, 2026-05-31)
ask n_feb: count(x in accounts on 2026-02-01)
ask n_jun: count(x in accounts on 2026-06-01)
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input gift_amt: money PLN
input gift_day: date
input pay_amt: money PLN
input pay_day: date

move gift: transfers
  on gift_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount gift_amt

move pay: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  gift_amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"
  gift_day = 2026-02-15 "plan"
  pay_amt = 200.00 PLN "plan"
  pay_day = 2026-04-15 "plan"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-05-31)
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-03-01..
place from_ana: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input gift_amt: money PLN
input gift_day: date
input pay_amt: money PLN
input pay_day: date

move gift_seen: transfers
  on gift_day
  leg cash from from_ana to konto amount gift_amt

move pay_seen: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from from_ana to konto amount pay_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  gift_amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"
  gift_day = 2026-02-15 "plan"
  pay_amt = 200.00 PLN "plan"
  pay_day = 2026-04-15 "plan"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-05-31)
=== expect k n_feb n_jun a.q b.q
k: ?"a.konto and b.konto are one, but the entry into accounts differs on 2026-02-15: 2026-01-01.. (a.konto) and 2026-03-01.. (b.konto)" (a.konto, b.konto)
  cut 2026-01-05
n_feb: ?"a.konto and b.konto are one, but the entry into accounts differs on 2026-02-01: 2026-01-01.. (a.konto) and 2026-03-01.. (b.konto)" (a.konto, b.konto)
  cut 2026-01-05
n_jun: 1
  cut 2026-01-05
a.q: 300.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-05
b.q: refused: RUN-LIFESPAN gift_seen.cash moves into or out of konto outside its lifespan
  cut 2026-01-05
